[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113363,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Canalicular adenoma is a benign salivary gland neoplasm of monomorphic epithelial cells arranged in anastomosing cords within a loose, vascularized stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113364,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8149/0 Canalicular adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113365,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.Z &amp; XH1TD7 Benign neoplasm of major salivary glands, unspecified &amp; Canalicular adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113366,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> canalicular tumour; canalicular mixed tumour; monomorphic adenoma, canalicular type; cystic adenoma; adenomatosis of accessory salivary glands.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113367,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113368,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Canalicular adenomas occur in the upper lip (80%), followed by the buccal mucosa, lower lip, hard palate, and soft palate {25141970}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113369,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with a slowly growing, mobile, painless, non-ulcerated mass {25141970}. Multifocal tumours are seen in 9% of cases {6281711; 8555146; 10102598; 15944978}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113370,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Canalicular adenoma accounts for &lt;&nbsp;1% of all salivary gland tumours {16053874; 17825603} and 4&ndash;6% of all benign minor salivary gland neoplasms {2845326; 7549761; 6281711; 9038559; 9563662; 10426199; 10769568; 16979373; 25141970; 22769409}. There is an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 1:1.7 {6366687; 25141970}, with a wide age range (33&ndash;91&nbsp;years) but a peak in the seventh decade of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113371,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113372,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p>Canalicular adenomas consistently lack the <em>IDH2</em> mutations of striated duct adenoma {36510691}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-22T14:15:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113373,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours range in size from 2&nbsp;to 30&nbsp;mm. They are well circumscribed, often cystic, showing light-yellow to tan to brown translucent nodules {25141970}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113374,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 73,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours have a bosselated or lobulated surface and are occasionally multifocal. The tumour cells are relatively monotonous, high cuboidal to columnar, and arranged in one or two cell layers. These layers anastomose to create a lattice of cords, canaliculi, tubules, and/or strands. Papillary projections into cystic spaces are common. The cell ribbons frequently abut one another (termed &ldquo;beading&rdquo;) with knots of cells joining parallel rows {6366687; 25141970}. The nuclei appear pseudostratified. Intraluminal squamoid morules may be seen in the canals. The nuclei are round to oval with coarse chromatin. There is a syncytial appearance to the cells. There is no basal or myoepithelial layer. The stroma is sparse, loose, fibrillary, and oedematous, and it sometimes contains histiocytes. Laminated microliths are frequently present {10583574; 25141970}. Mitoses are limited. Rare hybrid or collision tumours have been reported {8776422}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The cells are immunoreactive for pancytokeratin, CK7, S100, SOX10, and KIT (CD117), but non-reactive for DOG1, desmin, and actins {7534898; 10458827; 11337269; 12447671; 12738950; 15153875; 25141970}. There is a characteristic linear peripheral GFAP immunoreactivity {20614277; 25141970}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The entities in the differential diagnosis include basal cell adenoma, polymorphous adenocarcinoma, adenoid cystic carcinoma, reticulated myoepithelioma, selected odontogenic tumours, and skin basal cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:11:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
